          %h2#references References
          %p
            (For references on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-schemes"} dg-schemes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+schemes"} derived schemes
          %p The main references are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Derived+Algebraic+Geometry"} Derived Algebraic Geometry
            %li#LurieStructured
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} Structured Spaces
            %li#ToenVezzosi04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"} Gabriele Vezzosi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopical algebraic geometry II: geometric stacks and applications
                %strong 193
                (2008) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404373"}> arXiv:math/0404373
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/memo-193-902"} ams:memo-193-902
            %li#TV-HAG-to-DAG
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"} Gabriele Vezzosi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From HAG to DAG: derived moduli stacks
              %p
                NATO Sci. Ser. II Math. Phys. Chem., 131, Kluwer (2004) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0210407"}> math.AG/0210407
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The following notes deal with the theory modelled on coconnective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+dg-algebras"} commutative dg-algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Gaitsgory"}> Dennis Gaitsgory
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on geometric Langlands: stacks
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~gaitsgde/GL/Stackstext.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                J. Eugster and J. P. Pridham.
                = succeed "." do
                  %em An introduction to derived (algebraic) geometry
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/2109.14594"} arXiv
          %p
            The following notes deal with the theory modelled on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring+spectra"} E-infinity ring spectra
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+geometry"}> E-infinity geometry
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Applications of derived algebraic geometry to homotopy theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://webhomes.maths.ed.ac.uk/~cbarwick/papers/salamanca.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also the surveys
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher and derived stacks: a global overview
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Geometry Seattle 2005
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0604504"} arXiv:math/0604504
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/pspum/080.1"} doi:10.1090/pspum/080.1
            %li#VezzosiWhatIs
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"}> Gabriele Vezzosi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em What is a derived stack?
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/notices/201107/rtx110700955p.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Derived algebraic geometry
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1401.1044"} arxiv/1401.1044
          %p
            Discussion of
            %span.newWikiWord
              derived noncommutative algebra
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/derived+noncommutative+algebra"} ?
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-n+algebras"} E-n algebras
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"}> John Francis
                ,
                %em
                  Derived algebraic geometry over
                  = succeed "-Rings" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℰ
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_n
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/writ/thezrev.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"}> John Francis
                ,
                %em
                  The tangent complex and Hochschild cohomology of
                  = succeed "-rings" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
